         ],
         "text": [
            {
               "text": "#### Objects\n\nAcross this large region, we find metates — used to grind corn — like the one in the photo, in several museums.",
               "source": [],
               "date_time": null,
               "isTable": false,
               "imgdesc": "",
               "format": "markdown",
               "PostMention": ""
            },
            {
               "text": "<img src=\"http://www.historytracers.org/images/SanJoseCRMuseo/SanJoseCRAntropologia.jpg\" id=\"img0\" onclick=\"htImageZoom('img0', '0%')\"  class=\"imgcenter\"/>",
               "source": [],
               "date_time": [],
               "isTable": false,
               "imgdesc": "",
               "format": "html",
               "PostMention": ""
            },
            {
               "text": "*Photo taken in <htdate0></span>, during a visit to the Museum of Anthropology, San José, Costa Rica*",
               "source": [],
               "date_time": [
                  {
                     "type": "gregory",
                     "year": "2015",
                     "month": "10",
                     "day": "17"
                  }
               ],
               "isTable": false,
               "imgdesc": "",
               "format": "markdown",
               "PostMention": ""
            }
         ],
         "desc": null,
         "next": "ba0cae93-4516-4f24-a616-0c0d79372569",
         "prev": "",
         "jumpTo": "",
         "answer": null,
         "score": 1,
         "position": ""
      },
      {
         "id": "ba0cae93-4516-4f24-a616-0c0d79372569",
         "audio": "",
         "smile": "thinking",
         "source_menu": [],
         "text": [
            {
               "text": "Can we find out if these objects were made by the same people and taken to other regions — rather than made independently by different peoples?",
               "source": [],
               "date_time": null,
               "isTable": false,
               "imgdesc": "",
               "format": "markdown",
               "PostMention": ""
            }
         ],
         "desc": null,
         "next": "51c8e018-dd46-4bae-9a51-7af416dc31e0",
         "prev": "",
         "jumpTo": "",
         "answer": "yes",
         "score": 2,
         "position": ""
      },
      {
         "id": "51c8e018-dd46-4bae-9a51-7af416dc31e0",
         "audio": "",
         "smile": "shocking",
         "source_menu": [
            {
               "type": 1,
               "uuid": "3fb52297-2d42-46f2-8ef1-b8a2c8f4052a",
               "text": "HOOPES, J. W, pp. 459",
               "page": "https://www.researchgate.net/publication/225268005_Sorcery_and_the_Taking_of_Trophy_Heads_in_Ancient_Costa_Rica",
               "date_time": {
                  "type": "gregory",
                  "year": "",
                  "month": "",
                  "day": ""
               }
            },
            {
               "type": 1,
               "uuid": "ffffd208-eb09-4da3-b516-f8bc695758dd",
               "text": "Original Text",
               "page": "https://www.historytracers.org/index.html?page=class_content&arg=ffffd208-eb09-4da3-b516-f8bc695758dd",
               "date_time": {
                  "type": "gregory",
                  "year": "2026",
                  "month": "",
                  "day": ""
               }
            }
         ],
         "text": [
            {
               "text": "#### Beyond Appearances\n\nJust comparing height and width isn't enough. We also need to check the object's age — or the age of other items found with it.\n\nIn the case of the metates, extra evidence showed they were made in Costa Rica. And that's where most of them are found.",
               "source": [],
               "date_time": null,
               "isTable": false,
               "imgdesc": "",
               "format": "markdown",
               "PostMention": ""
            }
         ],
         "desc": null,
         "next": "1304d59e-9777-418e-a4d6-ddd3d57e34d5",
         "prev": "",
         "jumpTo": "",
         "answer": null,
         "score": 1,
         "position": ""
      },
      {
         "id": "1304d59e-9777-418e-a4d6-ddd3d57e34d5",
         "audio": "",
         "smile": "party",
         "source_menu": [],
         "text": [
            {
               "text": "#### Conclusion\n\nTo tell if something is equal, appearance alone isn't enough. You need to look at context — what's around it.\n\nWe used a Mesoamerican metate to see this in practice.",
               "source": [],
               "date_time": null,
               "isTable": false,
               "imgdesc": "",
               "format": "markdown",
               "PostMention": ""
            }
         ],
         "desc": null,
